  "id": "f5b80ca5-9f59-45b1-a549-166ed6375bf2",
  "title": "India and Mauritius Sign Long-Term Fuel Supply Agreement",
  "summary": "Indian Oil Corporation has signed a five-year agreement with Mauritius to supply its entire import requirement of petrol, diesel, and aviation turbine fuel. The agreement strengthens India’s role as a key energy partner in the Indian Ocean, while Mauritius aims to reduce reliance on foreign energy sources.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Indian Oil Corporation (IOC) will supply the entire import requirement of petrol, diesel, and aviation turbine fuel to Mauritius under a long-term agreement.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The agreement is part of a government-to-government memorandum of understanding (MoU) aimed at expanding oil and gas cooperation between India and Mauritius.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "India's public-sector oil marketing company will provide assured supplies and reduce exposure to price volatility.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
